    /// - [`ErrorKind::InvalidArgument`] (C++ `std::invalid_argument`): For an unknown source or malformed p/q lengths.
    /// - [`ErrorKind::Allocation`] (C++ `std::bad_alloc`): If owned parameter/assembly/result storage cannot be allocated.
