/// `this` is the C++ object: its virtual methods run the C++ implementation, as `datamunge::ode::RHS::method()` would in C++, so an override reaches the implementation it replaces through it. Each method's default does just that (for a method that is pure virtual in C++, it fails), so an implementation overrides only what it needs. Calling a virtual method on the object [`RHS::from_impl`] returns runs the Rust implementation.
